    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Lurelia features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Routines</p>

        <h3>Build flexible flows you can start, pause, resume, and finish</h3>

        <p>
          Create routines from ordered tasks, open detailed routine and task
          views, start a run full-screen, pause or resume active runs, and stop
          them when plans change. Reusable task templates reduce repeated setup,
          while Routine Contracts give important routines a more intentional
          commitment layer.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Routine Runs</span>
          <span>Task Templates</span>
          <span>Routine Contracts</span>
          <span>Pause & Resume</span>
          <span>Task Details</span>
          <span>Widgets</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Habits</p>

        <h3>Give repeated behavior its own place instead of hiding it inside a checklist</h3>

        <p>
          Lurelia includes a dedicated Habits area for building and tracking
          recurring behaviors over time. Habit detail and blueprint views keep the
          structure around each habit visible, while interactive widget support
          makes everyday completion easier to reach outside the main app.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Reminders</p>

        <h3>Keep one-off and recurring responsibilities visible without turning everything into a routine</h3>

        <p>
          Create scheduled reminders with dedicated detail views and notification
          support, including recurring reminders that remain active across cycles.
          Reminders can appear alongside the rest of your planning system and can
          also be acted on from Lurelia's interactive widgets and timeline tools.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Journeys</p>

        <h3>Break bigger personal goals into milestones and next steps you can actually move through</h3>

        <p>
          Journeys turn longer-term change into a structured path with a vision,
          milestones, steps, progress tracking, a current milestone, and a next
          action. Each Journey has its own detail experience so progress can build
          over time without getting flattened into a single task list.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Events</p>

        <h3>Plan regular and shared events without separating them from the rest of your life system</h3>

        <p>
          Lurelia's Events area supports local event planning, tags, detailed
          event views, week scheduling, calendar-style planning, and external
          calendar context. Shared Events add invitation links and QR codes,
          RSVP flows, host posts and announcements, comments, and management tools
          for events that involve other people.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Timeline & Kanban</p>

        <h3>Move between chronological planning and board-style organization without duplicating your work</h3>

        <p>
          The Timeline brings routine tasks, reminders, events, and other scheduled
          work into one execution-focused view. Kanban boards provide a second
          planning layer with columns and timeline access, letting you create,
          edit, complete, skip, or remove assigned work directly from the board
          while keeping it tied back to the same underlying items.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Planning Views</span>
            <strong>Connected</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Timeline</span>
            <span>Kanban</span>
            <span>Interactive Actions</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Act From the Same System</p>

        <h2>Planning works better when completing the work does not require rebuilding the plan somewhere else</h2>

        <p>
          Lurelia's Timeline, Kanban views, routine runs, detail screens, widgets,
          notifications, and App Shortcuts are designed to keep action close to
          planning. You can move from deciding what matters to actually completing
          it without turning the app into a passive list you only review later.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Lurelia planning preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Built for Action</span>

        <h4>Move from planning to doing without leaving the system.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Timeline</span>
          <strong>See what is due in chronological context</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Kanban</span>
          <strong>Move work through organized columns</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Widgets</span>
          <strong>Complete supported actions from the Home Screen</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Lurelia experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Routine Runs & Active Routine Banner</b>
              <small>Keep an active routine visible while moving through the rest of the app</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Started routines can remain visible through Lurelia's active-routine
            banner while you move through other tabs. Open the current run again,
            pause or resume it, and return to the same sequence without losing the
            run simply because you navigated elsewhere.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Routine Tasks, Templates & Contracts</b>
              <small>Build detailed routine structure without recreating common task setups</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Routine tasks have their own detail and editor flows, reusable task
            templates can speed up repeated setup, and Routine Contracts provide
            a dedicated place for the commitments attached to routines you want to
            define more explicitly.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Interactive Widgets & Notifications</b>
              <small>Keep routine, habit, reminder, and timeline actions available outside the main app</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Lurelia includes widget experiences for routines, habits, reminders,
            and the Kanban Timeline, with interactive actions where supported.
            Notification systems keep scheduled work visible even when you are not
            actively looking at the corresponding tab.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Events, Calendars & Week Scheduling</b>
              <small>See personal events in detailed, calendar, and week-based views</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Lurelia's Events area supports event creation and editing, tags,
            detail views, calendar-style planning, week scheduling, and external
            calendar context so scheduled commitments can live alongside routines,
            reminders, and habits.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Shared Events & Host Updates</b>
              <small>Invite people, collect RSVPs, publish updates, and keep conversation attached to the event</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Shared Events support links and QR codes, RSVP flows, host posts and
            announcements, rendered rich content, comments, and event management
            tools so coordination and updates can stay attached to the same event.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Journeys, Milestones & Steps</b>
              <small>Track longer-term progress without squeezing it into a daily checklist</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Journeys provide a separate structure for long-range goals, including
            a vision, milestones, ordered steps, completion progress, a current
            milestone, and a next step, with dedicated Journey detail pages for
            continuing that path over time.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Apple Shortcuts & Release Notes</b>
              <small>Connect routine data to automations and keep up with app changes</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            App Intents expose routine and routine-task information to Apple
            Shortcuts, including starting routines and retrieving routine details.
            Lurelia also includes release-note presentation inside the app so new
            changes can be surfaced after updates.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around Real Life</p>

        <h2>Different kinds of responsibilities need different structures without becoming different systems.</h2>

        <p>
          Lurelia is built around the fact that a routine, a reminder, a habit, an
          event, and a long-term Journey are not the same thing. Each gets its own
          structure, while Timeline, Kanban, widgets, notifications, and shared
          planning tools keep them connected enough to work as one system.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Lurelia</p>

      <h2>Keep routines, habits, reminders, events, and long-term plans connected without forcing them into the same shape.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Lurelia, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Lurelia/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Lurelia Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-lurelia-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .lurelia-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .floating-card span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .floating-card strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .floating-card-one {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .floating-card-two {
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    animation-delay: -2.4s;
  }

